--- body ---
## Context

Arena run 2026-10-29 (arena repo, docs/smoke-2026-10-29/README.md and
memory/journal/2026/2026-10-29-arena-run-smoke-and-free-panel.md): in the smoke
leg f1m (excursion scan HARNESS 1) the contestant read its own pinned `arena`
skill, a possible leak of the bench's method to the contestant.

Mechanism (read-only search, harness side): the contestant's skill set is the
Pi skills directories. `~/.pi/agent/skills/arena` is a symlink to the arena
repo's `skills/arena`, left over from the per-skill Pi links that `idh install`
created before PR 1690 (2026-10-27) moved Pi to the standard root. Pi now reads
`~/.agents/skills`, projected by `adapters/projections.json` (entry
`~/.agents/skills` -> `$IDH_ROOT/skills`, runtimes codex and pi, children).
The arena's `harness_pin.py` copies `skills/` from the live Pi agent dir into
the sealed snapshot, so whatever is linked at pin time is what the contestant sees.
The harness has no `skills/arena`: the link is not in the manifest, so
`idh install` neither declares nor retires it.

Status 2026-10-29 13:00Z: `~/.pi/agent/skills/` is empty; the stray link
is gone (removed by hand). No harness-side exclusion guard is wanted: the
cause was a one-off leftover, and a marker or deny list would be a guard
against a file that no longer exists (memory: no second-order guards).

Open question handed to the arena repo (arena ticket 1178): `harness_pin.py`
copies `~/.pi/agent/skills` (now empty) into the pin, while Pi reads
`~/.agents/skills` and the pin preserves `HOME`. A pinned contestant may
therefore see the live harness skills, unpinned. The pin code lives there.

## Scope

Harness side only: record the mechanism, and make `idh install` retire
pre-PR-1690 per-skill Pi links under `~/.pi/agent/skills` if it does not
already (dry-run first; if it already does, document only).

## Exit criteria

- [ ] The mechanism (pre-PR-1690 per-skill Pi link, outside the manifest, so never retired) is documented where `adapters/projections.json` or `idh install` is described.
- [ ] `idh install` retires or reports stale per-skill links under `~/.pi/agent/skills`, or the PR shows it already does.
- [ ] The arena-repo ticket on the pin source is cross-referenced here.
- [ ] `make check` passes.
